    "reviews": [
      {
        "reviewbody": "I had an original issue of this cookbook from my Grandma.  Lost in the floods of 2008 but glad to know there is some where I can still get chuckles at how recipes were written back in the early 1900s!",
        "reviewtitle": "wish I still had",
        "reviewer": "bakergal",
        "reviewdate": "2012-08-19 16:00:27",
        "createdate": "2012-08-19 16:00:27",
        "stars": "4"
      },
      {
        "reviewbody": "The foreward to the Betty Crocker Picture Cook Book of 1950 mentions this book as its predecessor. My mother and I believe my grandma had and used this cookbook, and remember its brown cover. Thanks to archive.com, I'm able to read its actual contents. It's a hoot to see recipes that start out with killing a turtle or chicken before cooking it! But the many of recipes for breads and salads etc. are still viable today, and I've been actually using some!",
        "reviewtitle": "We think my grandma had this cookbook",
        "reviewer": "judggy",
        "reviewdate": "2012-12-13 16:08:00",
        "createdate": "2012-12-13 16:08:00",
        "stars": "5"
      },
      {
        "reviewbody": "This was given to me by a good friend that has since passed on; I love the recipes, have used them a lot over the years, especially the cake and bread ones.",
        "reviewtitle": "I still have this original cookbook!!",
        "reviewer": "smurfette52",
